    "q-41478": {
      "dom_id": "step-q41478",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249580/assets/34ba4a4dcd6655d68fbc20fb6192354ae755cc7eaf14a2459e9b7012ffe6d9ea.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Given that $y=f(x)$ is periodic with period $4,$ what is the value of $f(62)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the period is $4,$ if we add (or subtract) any multiple of $4$ from the input, the output stays the same.\n\nSo, we can keep subtracting $4$ from the input until we get to an input that we see in the graph:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(62) & =f(62-4) \\\\  & =f(62-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =⋯ \\\\  & =f(62-15\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =f(2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-41478-a",
