    "q-51567": {
      "dom_id": "step-q51567",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249580/assets/4585ab21f7130a45e2ff5871e0fdc66cda5483181033010519781d9725eec36a.png)\n\nThe graph of a periodic function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. What is the period of this function?",
      "worked_solution": "Note that if we shift the graph $3$ units left or right, the graph remains unchanged.\n\nOn the other hand, if we shift the graph horizontally by any distance other than $3$ (or a multiple of $3$), we get a different graph.\n\nTherefore, the period of the function is $3.$",
