    "q-82379": {
      "dom_id": "step-q82379",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249580/assets/51ed86e455d0716953ad3d083646483d023ff7db6d8f45a9f27e4324d00b21db.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Given that $y=f(x)$ is periodic with period $4,$ what is the value of $f(-46)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the period is $4,$ if we add (or subtract) any multiple of $4$ from the input, the output stays the same.\n\nSo, we can keep adding $4$ to the input until we get to an input that we see in the graph:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-46) & =f(-46+4) \\\\  & =f(-46+2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =⋯ \\\\  & =f(-46+11\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =f(-2) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
